			<div class="content" id="post-content-1530520">
									

<p>I'm very interested, and don't have a problem with <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">any</span> most of the science,<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-425249-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-425249-1')">1</a></sup> but I'm not seeing how it's anomalous: there's not really anything here that depends on something particularly unnatural happening.</p>
<p>EDIT: Which is not to say that I don't still like this. I just don't see how it's the Foundation's problem.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-425249-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-425249-1')">1</a>. (There's a bit of a problem with &quot;SCP-1717-2 is an unknown substance that induces the expression of the SCP-1717-1 gene&quot; and &quot;A 20mg sample recovered from the same tank contained no identifiable SCP-1717-2&quot; both being in the same piece: if you don't know what it is, how could you tell whether it was present or not?)</div>
</div>

